# The map grade shader (0126, data/shaders/chaos_map_grade.frag) had no values to change. This adds five numbers the Lua
# module game_visualfx eases when the player crosses into another area (server weather opcode, field `m`):
#  * Lua: g_shaders.setMapGrade(tintR, tintG, tintB, saturation, contrast). Tint is added to the colour (0..1 scale),
#    saturation and contrast are added to the factors the shader already uses. All five 0 = the picture as before.
#    Each value is clamped (tint +-0.15, saturation and contrast +-0.35) and a NaN counts as 0.
#  * The values are atomics of ShaderManager (Lua thread writes, graphics thread reads); applyMapGrade() hands them to the
#    map shader as u_Params (0044) and a new u_Params2 (uniform id 18) right after the shader is bound, at the two map draw
#    sites. A map shader that does not declare them (the base's heat haze) simply ignores them.
#  * Nothing runs per frame beyond two uniform uploads when a map shader is set; with the grade option off no map shader
#    is set and nothing is uploaded.
